First Before going to start we will do setup an EKS Cluster

why because while creating an EKS Cluster it will take minimum 40 minutes time to create it

In this during particular time of 40 minutes we will do discuss project structure explanation

As of now we just created self managed clusters are what we created is kops cluster and minikube

these two are self managed type clusters

Now EKS is completly relates to cloud managed cluster

difference b/w both of them is kops & minikube comes under self managed clusters this both managed by us

EKS (ELASTIC KUBERNETES SERVICE) comes under in this EKS control-planel is managed by AWS and control-planel will not be visible for us 
only worker nodes we will do managed by us

go to official document once of eks aws -------> eneter

login to aws account

launch an one Instance for to create EKS ----------> name:myeks ---------> instance type: m7i-flex.large------> with keypair------> security groups:jenkins----->
attach IAM role o the instance ------------> ebs volume: 20 gb-------> launch instace and connect it

